  "assumptions": [
    "All reliability probabilities are synthetic sensitivity inputs, not vendor, operator or regulatory values.",
    "The per-HAPS independent availability value includes independently attributable planned maintenance and random platform faults but excludes the shared weather common-mode event.",
    "The HAPS fleet is unavailable when a shared HAPS-only weather event occurs or when every HAPS independently fails; HAPS platform failures are independent conditional on no shared event.",
    "Terrestrial and LEO backhaul are assumed independent of the HAPS weather event and independent of each other. Real correlated power, fibre, gateway, spectrum, cyber, space-weather and geopolitical failures can invalidate this assumption.",
    "Staggered planned maintenance is a policy constraint; because the example's per-platform availability already includes maintenance, maintenance downtime must not be subtracted a second time.",
    "The model treats a service zone as covered when at least one relevant provider is available; it does not model geographic overlap, radio capacity, latency, traffic load, group handover or partial service.",
    "Availability is an analytic probability over a one-year equivalent horizon, not a single simulated year or empirical confidence interval.",
    "A 99.99% target is a research objective only; it is not attributed to any operator and requires an SLA-defined service boundary and measured outage denominator.",
    "The five-year Sceye/SoftBank fleet agreement indicates movement toward fleet manufacture/launch/operations but does not itself disclose an achieved national availability SLA."
